    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0244" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg170"/>

                <head>Mr. Yeaman to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 5, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am now enabled to state, what you may
                    have learned from other sources, that by the treaty of peace between Austria and
                    Prussia, Austria has ceded to Prussia all of her joint rights in the two
                    duchies, with the condition that northern Schleswig is to be restored to
                    Denmark, if the people so wish. There is little doubt that a fair and
                    uninfluenced election will result in a restoration.</p>
                <p>The opinion is expressed here that the sentiment of the “Scandinavian” party is
                    gaining strength in Denmark, about which I am not sufficiently advised to speak
                    with certainty.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE H. YEAMAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
